  "notes": "Harlem punchline rap over Buckwild and Premier drums. Three parameters carry it. First, the whole-tone horn stab the research names is a real scale entry rather than a description — `whole_tone` sits in the table at low weight so it colours a minority of seeds, which is what \"occasional\" means. Second, the ghost snare is placed on `2a`, the 16th before beat 3 that the research names explicitly, and its probability is the highest on this axis — that stroke is the Buckwild signature here. Third, the bass genuinely walks a 3rd and a 5th and is described as prominent, so `independent_riff` with a low `followRootsProb` and `m3` in the passing tones, not a root-doubler. The melodic hook is scratched vocal fragments, so `timbreHint` is `chopped_vocal` rather than a keyboard. ⚠ `medium` because the research rates it medium-high and says the artist-side tempo is catalog-level: the BPM window is the one genuinely inferred parameter here, and the drum grammar behind it is documented producer workflow. ⚠ `halfStepDissonance` at 0.18 is authored from \"sinister two-note piano/organ motifs\" — it is well below the Mobb Deep end of the axis and well above the Buckwild jazz end. ⚠ The bass ceiling came down from 47 to 44 so it stays under a chord part that starts at 45 — `coherence.rs` requires the highest bass note to sit at or below the lowest chord note, and this model overlapped by 3.",
